  "rationale": "Deployed defences set mfa_admin and segmented true; all other defences (patched_*, mfa_user, mfa_dbadmin) remain false. The attacker can still get deep into the network: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user, escalate_workstation gives admin_workstation, and that lets pivot_internal bypass segmentation to reach_internal. From there auth_appserver gives foothold_appserver, kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin, and escalate_appserver gives admin_appserver. The chain breaks at the domain controller. auth_dc requires NOT mfa_admin, which is blocked, and it is the only way to get foothold_dc. Without foothold_dc, escalate_dc cannot give admin_dc, so dump_dbadmin_dc cannot give stolen_dbadmin, and nothing else produces stolen_dbadmin. Without stolen_dbadmin, auth_db and auth_fileserver are blocked. So there is no foothold or admin on the database or file server, and neither exfiltrate_db nor exfiltrate_fileserver can fire. exfiltrated is unreachable."
